  <section class="ai-market-shift">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="section-label">Why this matters now</div>
      <h2>AI prospecting is mainstream. Qualified conversations are still hard.</h2>
      <div class="ai-stat-grid">
        <div class="ai-stat-card">
          <strong>87%</strong>
          <span>of sales organizations use some form of AI for work such as prospecting, forecasting, lead scoring, or drafting emails.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ai-stat-card">
          <strong>55%</strong>
          <span>of sales professionals are already using AI for prospecting, with another 38% planning to do so.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ai-stat-card">
          <strong>34%</strong>
          <span>is the expected reduction in prospect-research time once sales agents are fully implemented.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="ai-source-note">Source: <a href="https://www.salesforce.com/news/stories/state-of-sales-report-announcement-2026/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">Salesforce, State of Sales 2026</a>.</p>
      <div class="ai-market-copy">
        <p>That adoption does not mean every company suddenly has a healthy pipeline. Most teams still face the same hard questions: Which accounts deserve attention? Is the data usable? Who owns the problem? Does the signal mean anything? Can someone reach the buyer? Is there enough interest for a real next step?</p>
        <p>AI can compress the research. It can help organize the clues. It can make a large market easier to inspect. But B2B pipeline still moves through relevance, timing, trust, judgment, follow-up, and live conversation.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="problem">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-label">The gap in the market</div>
      <h2>You do not need another robot spraying cold emails.</h2>
      <p>Many AI lead generation companies sell the dream of a fully autonomous SDR. Upload a market, switch on an agent, and wait for the calendar to fill.</p>
      <p>That pitch skips the hard part. Bad targeting can be automated. Weak data can be enriched with more weak data. Shallow personalization can be produced at enormous scale. A signal can be mistaken for a buyer. A booked meeting can still be a bad meeting.</p>
      <div class="punch">CallTeam uses modern intelligence without removing experienced human judgment from the sale.</div>
    </div>
  </section>

