  <section id="faq">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="section-label">AI lead generation FAQ</div>
      <h2>Questions B2B buyers ask before hiring an AI-assisted lead generation company.</h2>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3>What are AI lead generation services?</h3>
          <p>AI lead generation services use artificial intelligence and sales data to support prospect discovery, account research, data enrichment, intent-signal analysis, lead prioritization, outreach preparation, qualification, and appointment setting. At CallTeam, AI supports the intelligence layer while experienced people handle live cold calls and sales conversations.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3>How does CallTeam use AI for B2B lead generation?</h3>
          <p>CallTeam can use AI-assisted research and modern sales intelligence to clarify the ICP, discover best-fit accounts, identify decision-makers, organize available intent signals, enrich prospect data, prioritize accounts, prepare call angles, and structure qualification notes. Human callers then make the calls, confirm what is real, qualify the opportunity, and book the next step.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3>Is CallTeam an AI SDR or chatbot company?</h3>
          <p>No. CallTeam is not positioned as an autonomous AI SDR, chatbot, or mass cold-email system. AI works in the background to improve targeting, research, prioritization, and call preparation. Experienced people handle the live conversation.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3>Does CallTeam use AI for cold calling?</h3>
          <p>CallTeam uses AI to support the work around cold calling, including account research, lead prioritization, call preparation, message angles, note organization, and campaign learning. The calls themselves are handled by people who can listen, respond, qualify, and use judgment.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3>What is AI-assisted appointment setting?</h3>
          <p>AI-assisted appointment setting uses data and artificial intelligence to improve prospect selection, research, timing, qualification preparation, and follow-up organization. At CallTeam, a human caller earns the conversation and books an appropriate next step based on agreed qualification criteria.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3>Can AI identify companies that are ready to buy?</h3>
          <p>AI can help surface and organize signals that may make an account more relevant, but no signal proves that a company is ready to buy. Hiring, leadership changes, funding, technology changes, website activity, CRM engagement, relevant news, and third-party intent data can guide prioritization. A real conversation is still needed to confirm fit, interest, timing, and need.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3>What types of intent signals can support AI prospecting?</h3>
          <p>Depending on the market, tools, data access, and campaign, signals can include first-party website activity, CRM history, content engagement, hiring, funding, leadership changes, expansion, technology changes, job postings, relevant company news, and available third-party research intent. Signal quality varies and should be reviewed in context.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3>Can CallTeam build a B2B prospect list from scratch?</h3>
          <p>Yes. CallTeam can help define the ideal customer profile and build a targeted B2B prospect list around industries, company size, geography, buyer roles, account characteristics, relevant signals, and best-fit companies. Data can then be enriched, reviewed, prioritized, and prepared for calling.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3>Can CallTeam work with leads already in our CRM?</h3>
          <p>Yes. CallTeam can help segment and follow up with old CRM leads, dormant opportunities, inbound leads, event leads, webinar leads, referral lists, LinkedIn prospects, and target accounts. AI-assisted analysis can help organize the list, while human outreach determines which opportunities are still real.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3>What is the difference between AI lead generation software and an AI lead generation service?</h3>
          <p>Software gives your team a tool for data, research, scoring, enrichment, outreach, or workflow. A service helps execute the work. CallTeam connects the intelligence layer to human cold calling, follow-up, qualification, appointment setting, reporting, and campaign improvement.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3>Does AI replace human salespeople in lead generation?</h3>
          <p>AI can reduce manual research, organize data, and help teams prioritize. It does not replace the human skills needed in a live sales conversation, including listening, judgment, objection handling, trust, qualification, redirection, and deciding the right next step.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3>How does CallTeam qualify an AI-assisted lead?</h3>
          <p>Qualification criteria are agreed before the campaign. Depending on the offer, CallTeam can look for company fit, role relevance, business need, interest, timing, current process, authority path, and next-step potential. A data signal alone is not treated as a qualified lead.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3>How should AI lead generation performance be measured?</h3>
          <p>Measure reachable decision-makers, useful live conversations, qualification quality, appointments that meet the agreed criteria, follow-up completion, sales acceptance, pipeline movement, segment performance, and the reasons prospects say yes, no, or not now. Raw contact volume is not enough.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3>Who is CallTeam's AI lead generation service for?</h3>
          <p>The service is built for B2B founders, sales leaders, SaaS and technology companies, agencies, consultants, professional services firms, and other teams that need better-fit prospects, human cold calling, qualified conversations, and booked appointments without adding another disconnected sales tool.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3>How do we start?</h3>
          <p>Start with a free strategy call. CallTeam will look at your market, offer, current lists, CRM, available data, sales motion, qualification standard, and appointment goals to identify the right starting point.</p>
        </article>
